{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Devtools provides you with an easy-to-use and modular client that allows you to compose multiple devtools into one easy-to-use panel."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tanstack/vue-devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Devtools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" library. This will install the devtools core as well as provide you with the Vue-specific adapter."}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i @tanstack/vue-devtools","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next, in the root of your application, import the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" component from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/vue-devtools"},{"type":"text","value":" and add it to your template."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <App />\n  <TanStackDevtools />\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import the desired devtools and provide them to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" component via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"},{"type":"text","value":" prop along with a label for the menu."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Currently TanStack offers:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueQueryDevtoolsPanel"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport type { TanStackDevtoolsVuePlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport { VueQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/vue-query-devtools'\n\nconst plugins: TanStackDevtoolsVuePlugin[] = [\n  {\n    name: 'Vue Query',\n    component: VueQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n  },\n]\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <App />\n  <TanStackDevtools\n    :eventBusConfig=\"{ connectToServerBus: true }\"\n    :plugins=\"plugins\"\n  />\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note: The Vue adapter uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"},{"type":"text","value":" in plugin definitions. In Vue, components are passed as component references rather than JSX elements, and any additional props can be provided via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"},{"type":"text","value":" field."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finally, add any additional configuration you desire to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" component. More information can be found under the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Devtools Configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" section."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A complete working example can be found in our "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/devtools/latest/docs/framework/vue/examples/basic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"basic example"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"setup","text":"Setup","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Devtools provides you with an easy-to-use and modular client that allows you to compose multiple devtools into one easy-to-use panel.\n\n## Setup\n\nInstall the [TanStack Devtools](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tanstack/vue-devtools) library. This will install the devtools core as well as provide you with the Vue-specific adapter.\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/vue-devtools\n```\n\nNext, in the root of your application, import the `TanStackDevtools` component from `@tanstack/vue-devtools` and add it to your template.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <App />\n  <TanStackDevtools />\n</template>\n```\n\nImport the desired devtools and provide them to the `TanStackDevtools` component via the `plugins` prop along with a label for the menu.\n\nCurrently TanStack offers:\n\n- `VueQueryDevtoolsPanel`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport type { TanStackDevtoolsVuePlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport { VueQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/vue-query-devtools'\n\nconst plugins: TanStackDevtoolsVuePlugin[] = [\n  {\n    name: 'Vue Query',\n    component: VueQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n  },\n]\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <App />\n  <TanStackDevtools\n    :eventBusConfig=\"{ connectToServerBus: true }\"\n    :plugins=\"plugins\"\n  />\n</template>\n```\n\n> Note: The Vue adapter uses `component` instead of `render` in plugin definitions. In Vue, components are passed as component references rather than JSX elements, and any additional props can be provided via the `props` field.\n\nFinally, add any additional configuration you desire to the `TanStackDevtools` component. More information can be found under the [TanStack Devtools Configuration](../../configuration) section.\n\nA complete working example can be found in our [basic example](https://tanstack.com/devtools/latest/docs/framework/vue/examples/basic).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Basic setup\nid: basic-setup\n---\n\nTanStack Devtools provides you with an easy-to-use and modular client that allows you to compose multiple devtools into one easy-to-use panel.\n\n## Setup\n\nInstall the [TanStack Devtools](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tanstack/vue-devtools) library. This will install the devtools core as well as provide you with the Vue-specific adapter.\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/vue-devtools\n```\n\nNext, in the root of your application, import the `TanStackDevtools` component from `@tanstack/vue-devtools` and add it to your template.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <App />\n  <TanStackDevtools />\n</template>\n```\n\nImport the desired devtools and provide them to the `TanStackDevtools` component via the `plugins` prop along with a label for the menu.\n\nCurrently TanStack offers:\n\n- `VueQueryDevtoolsPanel`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport type { TanStackDevtoolsVuePlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-devtools'\nimport { VueQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/vue-query-devtools'\n\nconst plugins: TanStackDevtoolsVuePlugin[] = [\n  {\n    name: 'Vue Query',\n    component: VueQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n  },\n]\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <App />\n  <TanStackDevtools\n    :eventBusConfig=\"{ connectToServerBus: true }\"\n    :plugins=\"plugins\"\n  />\n</template>\n```\n\n> Note: The Vue adapter uses `component` instead of `render` in plugin definitions. In Vue, components are passed as component references rather than JSX elements, and any additional props can be provided via the `props` field.\n\nFinally, add any additional configuration you desire to the `TanStackDevtools` component. More information can be found under the [TanStack Devtools Configuration](../../configuration) section.\n\nA complete working example can be found in our [basic example](https://tanstack.com/devtools/latest/docs/framework/vue/examples/basic).\n"}
